    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42f968ba_12ac4752",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-20T18:05:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not in this CL, but we eventually need to distinguish creation and running of a VM. Creating a VM is defining a VM and make it persistent (until it gets deleted). Definition of a VM includes the various disk images (including the instance image and the userdata image) that the VM will use.\n\nRunning a VM is starting a crosvm process. It is stopped when either the VM voluntarily shuts itself down, or the client that started the VM goes out of scope (i.e. killed). \n\nThe disk images should be persistent; i.e. survive VM restarts and even host Android restarts. Otherwise, we wouldn\u0027t accumulate data in a pVM over a long period. They images shall be deleted when the VM is deleted, which could happen when the client explicitly requested or the client (app) is uninstalled.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bf0e5df_c7048682",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-21T12:34:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is not possible with the model of passing images as file descriptors, as file descriptors are not persistent.\n\nThat doesn\u0027t mean that you can\u0027t have persistent data in a VM though. The images you want to be persistent just need to be created in the client application or service, and then if you pass (a file descriptor to) the same image each time, you\u0027ll get the same data.",
      "parentUuid": "42f968ba_12ac4752",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13df643c_6300c519",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T09:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the disk images shall be passed as FDs. What I am saying here is that virt manager should provide distinct functions for creating and running a VM.\n\nDo you think that the creation of a VM (which includes the creation of the composite disk images, qcow2 images, etc.) should be done by the apps instead?",
      "parentUuid": "6bf0e5df_c7048682",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21452ffb_b568a5ad",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T17:37:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see how that is possible, if we want to pass everything as file descriptors, because the composite image refers to the partition images by filename (so here I\u0027m using names of the form /proc/self/fd/N, which rely on knowing the file descriptor number, and it remaining the same between creating the image and running it). If you have a suggestion for how to do this then we can discuss it tomorrow at the userspace sync-up.",
      "parentUuid": "13df643c_6300c519",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30507333_8ddd472c",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-20T18:55:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is dealing with untrsuted input, you may want to consider running in a minijail / without privileges (see go/rule-of-2).  Or probably better, make it a library to run in the client process?  No need to deal with it in this CL though.\n\nThis is also kind of aligned with Jiyong\u0027s suggestion to distinguish creation and running.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95eb125c_11511e83",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-21T12:34:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can\u0027t be in the client process, because it needs to refer to file descriptors in this process, to be able to pass them to crosvm.",
      "parentUuid": "30507333_8ddd472c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41a87fdf_9d4b00bf",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-21T16:11:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see.  IIUC, we\u0027d need to pass one FD that the backing content refers to another FD by /proc/self/fd/$N (for the actual private image).  I guess it\u0027s still possible if we are willing to assume the FD can\u0027t change?\n\nBTW, which uid will crosvm eventually run with?  If it requires privileges to setup, could it drop privileges and change to app uid afterward?  If these are actually possible, it could make the above easier.",
      "parentUuid": "95eb125c_11511e83",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58e7379c_086c8573",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T17:37:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The part that actually creates the composite disk image is a child process (mk_cdisk) which is just passed the config and the file descriptors it needs. This code is just checking the configuration and calling down to that (and is in safe Rust, so follows the rule of 2).\n\ncrosvm runs as the virtmanager UID, but in its own SELinux domain. We did discuss running it as the client UID, but people didn\u0027t seem keen on that, and there doesn\u0027t seem much point if all the images are passed as FDs anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "41a87fdf_9d4b00bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "442d69a7_dd6474ba",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T18:21:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "mk_cdisk still runs with the same privileges as the parent process, no?  That\u0027s why I suggested to put it in minijail with multiple options to de/minimize privileges.  Or is the plan to transit into another non-privileged domain?  But of course it\u0027s only relevant if you decide to not create the composite disk image in the client process.  Maybe a TODO based on the outcome of your discussion.",
      "parentUuid": "58e7379c_086c8573",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
