    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "817fdea3_bd43da84",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 197,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-21T12:34:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not? It\u0027s meaningless after the VM exits, because it refers to file descriptors which will no longer be open.",
      "parentUuid": "1b539148_e075a4f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09ee9efc_9e96aa27",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 197,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T09:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In case when the files referenced in this composite image file are file descriptors, yes, we need to delete this and create again when the same VM is re-started.\n\nHowever, what if the referenced files are not file descriptors but real paths? e.g. /apex/com.android.virt/etc/fs/microdroid_system.img? Letting app open the files, passing it via fd and then letting virt manager read the fd seem a little bit cumbersome. Virt manager already have access to the platform-owned filesystem images, in which case it can access them directly via paths. Passing fd makes sense when the filesystem images are owned by apps (e.g. a downloaded Ubuntu distro).",
      "parentUuid": "817fdea3_bd43da84",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d7486ac_c74d87c9",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 197,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T17:37:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "True, we could use the filesystem path for images that are readable by crosvm / VirtualizationService. I\u0027d prefer not to have two different ways of passing images though, as it means more complexity, more different combinations of configuration, and more chances for bugs. Treating all images the same way keeps things simpler and easier to reason about.",
      "parentUuid": "09ee9efc_9e96aa27",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 196,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "7f5e720b622eb607fa9157574306727697146290",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
